python/uv.lock text eol=lf
tests/conformance/** text eol=lf
cpp/** text eol=lf

# Vendored third-party sources are byte-identical to upstream and pinned by
# SHA-256 in cpp/VENDORED.md. -whitespace exempts them from the pre-commit
# `git diff --check` gate: Catch2's single header ends with a blank line, and
# "fixing" it would edit a file ADR-0002's vendoring rule forbids editing AND
# invalidate the recorded hash -- turning the pin into a lie to satisfy a house
# style rule that was never meant to apply to code we do not own.
#
# linguist-vendored keeps 650 kB of generated header out of GitHub's language
# statistics, so the repository still reads as Rust/Python/C++ rather than as a
# test framework.
cpp/third_party/** -whitespace linguist-vendored

# Byte-exact conformance oracles. Their content is whatever the decoders
# actually emit, so a trailing blank line is DATA, not a style slip: `dump --raw`
# with an offset past end of file legitimately ends with one -- the range header,
# then an empty hex block. Trimming it to satisfy `git diff --check` would make
# the oracle stop matching the output it exists to pin, which is the same
# reasoning that exempts the vendored sources above. `text eol=lf` from the rule
# further up still applies; only the whitespace check is switched off.
tests/conformance/expected/** -whitespace
